WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.860
Camera placement determines what the system can observe.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:11.800
Define the legitimate event first, then select a field of view that captures useful context without extending into private or unrelated areas.

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:17.660
Height, angle, distance, lens, and mounting stability affect detection quality.

4
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:25.220
Resolution controls image detail and increases bandwidth, decode work, storage, and inference cost.

5
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.840
Frame rate improves temporal coverage but may add little value for slow events.

6
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:35.500
Select each setting from the use case rather than using the maximum for every camera.

7
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:40.580
RTSP commonly delivers network video to NVRs and AI services.

8
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.720
Protect stream credentials and restrict which systems can connect.

9
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:51.580
Monitor stream age and decode errors so a frozen or delayed picture does not appear healthy.

10
00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:57.620
Many cameras provide a high-resolution main stream and a lower-resolution substream.

11
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:05.560
The substream can support motion or object filtering with lower compute, while the main stream is retained or sampled for detailed review.

12
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:11.260
Verify that the smaller stream still contains enough information for the chosen task.

13
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:20.340
Lighting, weather, glare, shadows, night illumination, occlusion, motion blur, and seasonal changes affect performance.

14
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:26.200
Evaluate placement and model results under representative conditions, not only during installation.

15
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:35.840
Reduce unnecessary data through privacy masks, regions of interest, schedules, frame sampling, and event-based processing.

16
00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.420
These controls can improve cost and alert relevance while limiting collection.

17
00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:47.480
Document camera purpose, permitted coverage, owner, stream settings, retention, and review access.
